course: dictionary
lesson: 874
title: One word, four meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one is meant. Look at the words around billy before you choose. Is it a thing, an animal, a name, or a tool?
explain: Australians use billy for a metal can with a lid and handle, used to boil water over a campfire to make tea. «A horse named Old Billy was reported to have lived to 62 in England in the 1800s.» Here Billy is a name, because the word named comes just before it.
explain: A billy goat is a male goat, and the fairy tale The Three Billy Goats Gruff uses that meaning. In the United States, a billy club is a short wooden stick carried by police. Billy can also be a short form of the name William, as in «Me and little Billy here, we was trying to find our way to school».
fact: A billy is a metal can with a lid and handle, used to boil water over a campfire.
fact: In Australia and New Zealand, billy tea is tea made in a billy.
fact: A billy goat is a male goat.
fact: A billy club is a short wooden stick carried by police, in the United States.
fact: Billy is a short form of the name William, so it can be a person's name.
exercise: In the song «Waltzing Matilda», a swagman waits while his billy boils. What is a billy here? | A male goat | A short wooden stick carried by police | A boy's nickname for his brother | *A metal can used to boil water
exercise: In the fairy tale The Three Billy Goats Gruff, what is a billy? | A wooden stick used by police | A metal can for boiling water | A boy called William | *A male goat
exercise: «A horse named Old Billy was reported to have lived to 62 in England in the 1800s.» How is Billy used here? | *As the name of a horse | A can for boiling water | A goat with a beard | A police club
test: Where might you boil water in a billy over a campfire? | On a train, to heat a sandwich | In a bathtub, to wash clothes | In a cold freezer, to make ice | *In Australia, to make a cup of tea
test: Billy is a short form of which name? | Richard | *William | Benjamin | Harold
exam: Which meaning of billy is a short wooden stick carried by police in the United States? | A nickname for William | A male goat | A metal can with a lid | *A billy club
